/-!
# Tag 0BLX in one statement

Let `A` be a ring, `I ⊂ A` a finitely generated ideal, `𝒞` a site, `𝒪` a sheaf of `A`-algebras
and `ℱ` a sheaf of `𝒪`-modules. [Stacks, Tag 0BLX] asserts
```
RΓ(𝒞, ℱ)^∧ = RΓ(𝒞, ℱ^∧)   in D(A),
```
the completion on the left along `I` and the one on the right along `I𝒪`, and that this produces
two spectral sequences
```
E₂^{i,j} = H^i(H^j(𝒞, ℱ)^∧)   and   E₂^{p,q} = H^p(𝒞, H^q(ℱ^∧)),
```
both converging to `H^*(RΓ(𝒞, ℱ)^∧) = H^*(𝒞, ℱ^∧)`.

This file assembles the three assertions into the single statement
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_iso_and_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections`, under the
source's own hypotheses and with both derived completion functors produced rather than assumed.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.nonempty_iso_derivedGlobalSectionsOverUnbounded_of_plus`:
  **`RΓ(𝒞, -)` on `D⁺(𝒪)` and on `D(𝒪)` agree on a bounded below complex.** Both are right
  derived functors of `Γ(𝒞, -)`, so both are computed by `Γ(𝒞, -)` on a bounded below complex of
  injectives, and a bounded below complex has such a resolution by [Stacks, Tag 013K].
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.nonempty_iso_siteCohomologyOver_homologyFunctor`:
  the same comparison at a sheaf, `H^j(𝒞, ℱ) ≅ H^j(RΓ(𝒞, ℱ[0]))`, which is what lets the
  cohomology of the site appear on the `E₂`-page of the first spectral sequence while the
  abutment is read off the unbounded `RΓ(𝒞, -)`.
* `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.bijective_precomp_adjunction_unit`: the universal property of a
  reflector onto a class of objects, in the elementary form that
  `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.isoOfReflection` consumes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_iso_and_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 0BLX].** It is the only declaration carrying that tag's attribute: the statements
  it assembles, each one assertion of the tag or a special case of one, are untagged —
  `exists_spectralSequence_derivedCompletion_globalSections` and
  `exists_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections` of `GlobalSectionsCompletion.lean`,
  `exists_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections_generatedIdealSheaf` of
  `GlobalSectionsCompletionGenerated.lean`, and the nilpotent-regime
  `exists_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedGlobalSections` of `UnboundedGlobalSections.lean` and
  `exists_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections_of_forall_isNilpotent` of
  `UnboundedGlobalSectionsSpectralSequence.lean`.

## The assembly

All three assertions are read with one and the same derived global sections functor on the
unbounded derived category, `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedGlobalSectionsOverUnbounded`,
so that the two spectral sequences converge to the cohomology of the two sides of the identity
on the nose.

*The ideal sheaf.* `I` is finitely generated, so `I = (a_1, …, a_r)`, and then `I𝒪` **is** the
ideal sheaf generated by the global sections `ρ a_1, …, ρ a_r` of `𝒪`:
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIdealSheafGeneratedBy_generatedIdealSheaf` together with the
uniqueness `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.eq_of_isIdealSheafGeneratedBy`, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_of_isIdealSheafGeneratedBy`. So the
whole statement is proved at the source's own `I𝒪`, and the generators are a presentation of it
rather than a condition on it. In particular [Stacks, Tag 099F], the existence of `(-)^∧` on
`D(𝒪)`, is produced from them by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf`.

*The identity.* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.nonempty_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedGlobalSections`
of `GlobalSectionsCompletionKoszulIdentity.lean`, at an arbitrary object of `D(𝒪)`, with the
module-side completion `DerivedCompletion.derivedCompletionFunctor A a` along
`Ideal.span (Set.range a) = I`. That functor is identified with the reflector carried by the
statement below by `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.isoOfReflection`: both are reflections of
`D(A)` onto the objects derived complete along `I`.

*The first spectral sequence.* [Stacks, Tag 0BKE],
`AdicFilteredCompletion.exists_spectralSequence_derivedCompletion_homology`, applied to
`RΓ(𝒞, ℱ)` — which is also where the reflector on `D(A)` comes from, by [Stacks, Tag 0920]. Its
`E₂`-page is `H^i` of the completion of `H^j(RΓ(𝒞, ℱ))[0]`, and
`nonempty_iso_siteCohomologyOver_homologyFunctor` rewrites `H^j(RΓ(𝒞, ℱ))` as `H^j(𝒞, ℱ)`.

*The second spectral sequence.*
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections` of
`GlobalSectionsCompletion.lean` — the spectral sequence of [Stacks, Tag 015J] for `Γ(𝒞, -)` read
through a Cartan-Eilenberg resolution — at the bounded below representative of `ℱ^∧` produced by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_plus_derivedCompletion_generatedIdealSheaf_obj`. Its
abutment is the cohomology of the bounded below `RΓ(𝒞, -)` at that representative, and
`nonempty_iso_derivedGlobalSectionsOverUnbounded_of_plus` rewrites it as the cohomology of
`RΓ(𝒞, ℱ^∧)` taken with the unbounded functor, which is the left hand side of the identity.

## Implementation notes

*Both completion functors are existentially quantified*, as reflectors onto the derived-complete
objects together with their adjunctions, for the reason the other statements of this directory do
the same: the library fixes no choice of either. On the sheaf side the witness is the reflector of
[Stacks, Tag 099F] and on the module side the one of [Stacks, Tag 0920]; neither is a hypothesis.

*The comparison of the two derived global sections functors.* `Γ(𝒞, -)` has a right derived
functor on `D⁺(𝒪)` (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedGlobalSectionsOver`, used by
[Stacks, Tag 015J] and by `H^p(𝒞, -)`) and one on the whole of `D(𝒪)`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedGlobalSectionsOverUnbounded`, which is what the derived
completion of a sheaf needs). On a bounded below complex they agree, and the proof is the
classical one: resolve by a bounded below complex of injectives, which is K-injective
(`CochainComplex.isKInjective_of_injective`), and on such a complex each of the two comparisons
`Γ(𝒞, J) ⟶ RΓ(𝒞, J)` is invertible —
`CategoryTheory.Functor.isIso_totalRightDerivedUnit_app_of_rightAcyclic` for the bounded below
functor and `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_moduleGlobalSectionsDerivedUnit_app` for the
unbounded one.

*The `Limits.HasProduct` and `Limits.HasCoproduct` instances* are completeness conditions on the
derived categories involved, of the same kind as those carried throughout this directory, and not
mathematical hypotheses on the data.

## References

